            <ArticleTitle>A sympathetic view on fat by leptin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>26-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cell.2015.09.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0092-8674(15)01177-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Zeng et al. reveal that the lipolytic effect of the hormone leptin is mediated by sympathetic nerve fibers that directly &quot;envelope&quot; white adipocytes. Local activation of the sympathetic input to the fat opens new venues to circumvent central leptin resistance in obesity.</AbstractText>
